		{"id":"203958752b31f374","type":"text","text":"For legacy on prem applications that use old protocols in authentications, Create replica domain controller in cloud as these applications won’t be able to join Entra ID","x":-4174,"y":-1546,"width":1344,"height":50},
		{"id":"e179790feea37559","type":"text","text":"Supports role-based access control (RBAC) for permissions.","x":-3871,"y":-2067,"width":530,"height":51},
		{"id":"4e63c713bc262ae6","type":"text","text":"Enables hybrid identity, allowing users to sign in with the same credentials across on-prem & cloud services.","x":-3619,"y":-1634,"width":894,"height":50},
		{"id":"4c7f52a5e90149e6","type":"text","text":"Microsoft 365 Groups (Formerly Office 365 Groups)","x":-3530,"y":-1804,"width":471,"height":50},
		{"id":"c5d8c778962d236f","type":"text","text":"A tool that syncs on-premises Active Directory (AD) with Microsoft Entra ID (Azure AD).","x":-3453,"y":-1699,"width":728,"height":50},
		{"id":"27a88943272e2eed","type":"text","text":"Can be synced from on-premises AD or created directly in Entra ID","x":-3912,"y":-1992,"width":571,"height":50},
		{"id":"304796d76fd16121","type":"text","text":"- Assigned – Manually add/remove members.\n- Dynamic – Users/devices automatically added based on rules (e.g., department = IT).","x":-4128,"y":-1920,"width":787,"height":76},
		{"id":"3db86011f9c3c31c","type":"text","text":"Security","x":-991,"y":-1315,"width":127,"height":50},
		{"id":"a13ce3411a797916","type":"text","text":"SKU","x":-165,"y":174,"width":101,"height":50},
		{"id":"e7872b42f94fcff4","type":"text","text":"Size","x":-11,"y":174,"width":101,"height":50},
		{"id":"0c7edd39f8a3820f","type":"text","text":"Table Storage","x":-1820,"y":3092,"width":172,"height":50},
		{"id":"df3a3a05710ff535","type":"text","text":"# Azure Storage Account Types\n\n| Type of Storage Account         | Supported Storage Services                                                        | Redundancy Options    | Usage                                                                                                                                        |\n| ------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Standard general-purpose v2** | Blob Storage (incl. Data Lake Storage), Queue Storage, Table Storage, Azure Files | LRS, GRS, RA-GRS, ZRS | Standard storage for most Azure Storage use cases. Supports blobs, file shares, queues, and tables. Use Premium File Shares for NFS support. |\n| **Premium block blobs**         | Blob Storage (incl. Data Lake Storage)                                            | LRS and ZRS           | Premium storage for block and append blobs. Ideal for high transaction rates, small objects, or low latency needs.                           |\n| **Premium file shares**         | Azure Files                                                                       | LRS and ZRS           | Premium storage for file shares. Best suited for enterprise or high-performance workloads. Supports both SMB and NFS.                        |\n| **Premium page blobs**          | Page blobs only                                                                   | LRS and ZRS           | Premium storage account for page blobs only.                                                                                                 |\n","x":-2875,"y":3184,"width":1323,"height":387},
		{"id":"4963e9e8e4261cde","type":"text","text":"# Azure Storage Redundancy Options Comparison\n\n|Redundancy Type|Full Name|How It Works|Pros|Cons|Use Case|Cost|\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|**LRS**|Locally Redundant Storage|Data replicated 3 times within a single datacenter|- Cheapest option  <br>- Protects against hardware failures|- Doesn't protect against datacenter failures|Workloads with low durability needs, cost-sensitive applications|Lowest|\n|**ZRS**|Zone-Redundant Storage|Data synchronously replicated across 3 availability zones in same region|- Protects against zone failures  <br>- High availability|- More expensive than LRS  <br>- Not available in all regions|Business-critical applications needing regional high availability|Moderate|\n|**GRS**|Geo-Redundant Storage|Data replicated 3 times in primary region + asynchronously to secondary region|- Protects against datacenter and regional disasters  <br>- Good for disaster recovery|- Higher cost  <br>- Secondary region not accessible unless failover occurs|Disaster recovery and business continuity|Higher|\n|**GZRS**|Geo-Zone-Redundant Storage|Combines ZRS (3-zone replication in primary) with GRS (geo-replication to secondary)|- Highest durability  <br>- Protects against zone, datacenter, and region failures|- Most expensive option|Mission-critical workloads requiring highest availability|Highest|\n|**RA-GRS**|Read-Access Geo-Redundant Storage|Like GRS but allows read access to secondary region at all times|- Geo-distributed apps with read access to secondary  <br>- Faster disaster recovery|- More expensive than GRS/GZRS|Read-heavy apps needing global access and disaster recovery|Higher than GRS|\n|**RA-GZRS**|Read-Access Geo-Zone-Redundant Storage|Like GZRS but allows read access to secondary region at all times|- Combines benefits of GZRS with read access to secondary|- Most expensive option with read access|Mission-critical read-heavy apps needing global access|Highest with read access|","x":-3331,"y":3639,"width":1731,"height":582},
		{"id":"0fab050d9a280e75","type":"text","text":"Account Replication","x":-1409,"y":3880,"width":216,"height":50},
		{"id":"1e322262d2904ed2","type":"text","text":"Account Types","x":-1376,"y":3258,"width":183,"height":50},
		{"id":"490b651f1dff0232","type":"text","text":"Storage","x":-967,"y":2999,"width":135,"height":50},
		{"id":"1986ca647dd29091","type":"text","text":"🔹 Supports Linux & UNIX clients.\n🔹 Requires Premium File Storage.\n🔹 Best for high-performance applications & container workloads.","x":-3337,"y":2480,"width":579,"height":100},
		{"id":"563252490cd0be08","type":"text","text":"🔹 Supports Windows & Linux clients.\n🔹 Works with Azure AD & on-prem AD authentication.\n🔹 Suitable for general-purpose file sharing & app storage.","x":-3303,"y":2355,"width":508,"height":100},
		{"id":"7fb44fdfdf2674d2","type":"text","text":"|**Tier**|**Best for**|**Performance**|**Cost**|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|Transaction Optimized|Frequent access|Medium latency|Medium|\n|Hot|Infrequent access|Standard performance|Low|\n|Cool|Rare access, archival|Higher latency|Lowest|","x":-3039,"y":2610,"width":707,"height":150},
		{"id":"fd8e5a8325563034","type":"text","text":"SMB (Server Message Block) File Shares ","x":-2731,"y":2380,"width":399,"height":50},
		{"id":"c36fea9dd43b23c5","type":"text","text":"NFS (Network File System) File Shares ","x":-2693,"y":2505,"width":361,"height":50},
		{"id":"5aeb45b1a7a0e170","type":"text","text":"Fully managed file shares in the cloud.","x":-2486,"y":2230,"width":399,"height":50},
		{"id":"7217985cece335b5","type":"text","text":"Supports authentication with Azure AD & Active Directory.","x":-2595,"y":2305,"width":508,"height":50},
		{"id":"ac0b1b4b0902e212","type":"text","text":"Types","x":-2212,"y":2430,"width":125,"height":50},
		{"id":"14f8ca1c1e6a68a3","type":"text","text":"File Storage","x":-1818,"y":2510,"width":170,"height":50},
