		{"id":"9a9f8eeb614fc520","type":"text","text":"Queue Storage","x":-1846,"y":2994,"width":198,"height":50},
		{"id":"c3f3fea2ac811f9d","type":"text","text":"Storage Types","x":-1376,"y":2272,"width":179,"height":50},
		{"id":"f37f674b912240e3","type":"text","text":"Delete","x":-3396,"y":2007,"width":125,"height":50},
		{"id":"cb416fc4955ecb9b","type":"text","text":"Archive","x":-3224,"y":2007,"width":124,"height":50},
		{"id":"554e41719b90ea9b","type":"text","text":"Cold","x":-2872,"y":2007,"width":109,"height":50},
		{"id":"07e2e94d07b0e34c","type":"text","text":"Cool","x":-2595,"y":2007,"width":109,"height":50},
		{"id":"cb7061128c7df345","type":"text","text":"Hot","x":-2332,"y":2007,"width":112,"height":50},
		{"id":"052cb6b5561f82c9","type":"text","text":"Blob Snapshots","x":-2473,"y":1263,"width":187,"height":50},
		{"id":"166500ab94d37188","type":"text","text":"Blob Versioning","x":-2494,"y":1325,"width":208,"height":50},
		{"id":"e65e17c2d6b088c3","type":"text","text":"Immutable Blob Storage","x":-2536,"y":1388,"width":250,"height":50},
		{"id":"0b60f83455b88568","type":"text","text":"|**Tier**|**Access Frequency**|**Performance**|**Storage Cost**|**Access Cost**|**Best For**|\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|**Hot**|Frequently accessed|Fastest access time|Higher|Lower|Active applications, frequently used documents/images/logs, web/mobile content|\n|**Cool**|Every 30+ days|Slightly slower than Hot|Moderate|Moderate|Backup/disaster recovery, less frequently accessed data, occasional analysis|\n|**Cold**|Every 90+ days|Slower than Cool, faster than Archive|Lower than Cool|Higher than Archive|Long-term backups with occasional retrieval, compliance data, rare-access datasets|\n|**Archive**|Months/years (rarely)|Very slow (hours to retrieve)|Lowest|Highest|Compliance/regulatory archives, historical data, long-term backups|","x":-3303,"y":1483,"width":1033,"height":360},
		{"id":"824ebee51874a06d","type":"text","text":"Lifecycle Policies","x":-2217,"y":1905,"width":196,"height":50},
		{"id":"f747d429975b981a","type":"text","text":"Date Protection","x":-2206,"y":1313,"width":185,"height":50},
		{"id":"a39af75bf7b432c5","type":"text","text":"Access Tiers","x":-2187,"y":1692,"width":166,"height":50},
		{"id":"33a8579702c4fcc2","type":"text","text":"Blob Storage","x":-1820,"y":1217,"width":170,"height":50},
		{"id":"dcd883b74cdee866","type":"text","text":"Uses Azure AD tokens to grant access to Azure Storage.","x":-3581,"y":847,"width":524,"height":50},
		{"id":"d8e3d80a955877ba","type":"text","text":"Supports role-based access control (RBAC) with predefined and custom roles","x":-3709,"y":907,"width":652,"height":50},
		{"id":"d83ef57161406a52","type":"text","text":"Azure Storage Explorer is a free, standalone desktop application that\nallows you to manage Azure Storage resources visually without needing to\nuse the Azure Portal. It provides a GUI-based interface to interact with\nvarious storage services.","x":-3410,"y":993,"width":654,"height":130},
		{"id":"a9aa3d52ea2f1e9e","type":"text","text":"Access it Using Access key, SAS Token for extra security or by your Entra ID user account with the needed RBAC privilege.","x":-3749,"y":1148,"width":992,"height":50},
		{"id":"757e98da74dc9c9e","type":"text","text":"Azure Storage Explorer","x":-2659,"y":1123,"width":255,"height":50},
		{"id":"67fec87e1967ad49","type":"text","text":"Anonymous Public Access through public endpoint (URL)","x":-2906,"y":449,"width":502,"height":50},
		{"id":"aa50665ef3bbdd7d","type":"text","text":"Storage Account Access Keys","x":-2700,"y":595,"width":296,"height":50},
		{"id":"a307494c5cb24bc7","type":"text","text":"Access Techniques","x":-2234,"y":670,"width":213,"height":50},
		{"id":"198227307dbc91de","type":"text","text":"Shared Access Signature (SAS) Tokens","x":-2779,"y":728,"width":375,"height":50},
		{"id":"a0ec7d3674c527b1","type":"text","text":"Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) Authentication (Recommended)","x":-2974,"y":882,"width":570,"height":50},
		{"id":"399212ac80b59b86","type":"text","text":"No authentication required.","x":-3277,"y":474,"width":272,"height":50},
		{"id":"7902b797b8089382","type":"text","text":"Each storage account has two 512-bit access keys","x":-3243,"y":558,"width":455,"height":50},
		{"id":"be533bb6333b0bf1","type":"text","text":" Provides full control over all services in the account.","x":-3245,"y":620,"width":457,"height":50},
		{"id":"b3691ff84b296247","type":"text","text":"Generates a temporary URL with limited permissions for a specific time.","x":-3474,"y":703,"width":608,"height":50},
		{"id":"a6797fcde9fadb9c","type":"text","text":"Can restrict access by IP address, permissions, and expiration.","x":-3416,"y":777,"width":550,"height":50},
		{"id":"7e304bc03c14eb2b","type":"text","text":"Enables public read access to blobs or containers.","x":-3450,"y":399,"width":445,"height":50},
		{"id":"5d472ab2efa4fea1","type":"text","text":"Snapshot","x":-2470,"y":2779,"width":138,"height":50},
		{"id":"4252e10dcba57b8f","type":"text","text":"Soft Delete","x":-2491,"y":2854,"width":159,"height":50},
		{"id":"0f25254341795803","type":"text","text":"keeping deleted file shares recoverable for a retention period.","x":-3105,"y":2854,"width":549,"height":50},
		{"id":"820cbebbb3e29a3f","type":"text","text":"Data Protection","x":-2270,"y":2804,"width":183,"height":50},
		{"id":"883d0c2b0c407d1d","type":"text","text":"How to Copy Data to Azure","x":-1132,"y":4411,"width":272,"height":54},
		{"id":"28f1831ecce54ecc","type":"text","text":"| Method                   | Best For                          | Speed      | Automation | Use Case                                                                 |\n|--------------------------|-----------------------------------|------------|------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Azure Portal             | Small data uploads               | Slow       | No         | Uploading files manually                                                |\n| AzCopy (CLI)             | Large datasets                   | Fast       | Yes        | Automated, script-based transfers                                       |\n| Azure Storage Explorer   | Medium datasets                  | Medium     | No         | Drag-and-drop interface for files                                       |\n| Azure Import/Export      | Large offline data transfers      | High       | Yes        | Moving TBs of data via shipped disks                                    |\n| Azure Data Box           | Massive data (PB-scale)           | Very High  | Yes        | Bulk migration (TBs/PBs), data center shutdown, disaster recovery        |","x":-2483,"y":4291,"width":1207,"height":225},
		{"id":"b1d6e1c4dbc89fd4","type":"text","text":"Supports VM backups, SQL databases, file shares, and SAP HANA.","x":1309,"y":3208,"width":588,"height":50},
		{"id":"dad7e4ce96ac6751","type":"text","text":"Backup Components\n- Azure Recovery Services Vault – Stores & manages backup data\n- Azure Backup Center – Centralized backup monitoring & management","x":1309,"y":3266,"width":637,"height":126},
		{"id":"e2bb142fd3d1374e","type":"text","text":"Provides disaster recovery as a service (DRaaS).","x":1441,"y":2701,"width":437,"height":50},
		{"id":"6f5bb9c8a7bb5b35","type":"text","text":"Replicates workloads from on-premises or Azure region to another.","x":1441,"y":2776,"width":613,"height":50},
		{"id":"43a647f8c66d7d88","type":"text","text":"How Does ASR Work?\n1️⃣ Replication: Continuously replicates VMs & workloads\n2️⃣ Monitoring: Tracks health & compliance\n3️⃣ Failover: Switchover to Azure in case of disaster\n4️⃣ Failback: Return to the original site when resolved","x":1441,"y":2849,"width":515,"height":169},
		{"id":"42d351c2f64eb429","type":"text","text":"Supported Scenarios:\n✔ On-premises → Azure\n✔ Azure region → Another Azure region\n✔ VMware, Hyper-V, Physical Servers","x":1441,"y":3040,"width":391,"height":132},
		{"id":"e676df01c4cd2c01","type":"text","text":"Azure Site Recovery (ASR)","x":1033,"y":2849,"width":285,"height":50},
		{"id":"17a88bf4eff2c39f","type":"text","text":"Azure Backup","x":1033,"y":3273,"width":187,"height":50},
		{"id":"c6cc6615e903b96f","type":"text","text":"Azure Availability Zones and Azure Availability Set","x":1033,"y":3440,"width":454,"height":50},
		{"id":"a9646ea20ff5e6e5","type":"text","text":"The maximum allowable downtime","x":1648,"y":2485,"width":348,"height":50},
		{"id":"947d43b4d2be0715","type":"text","text":"The maximum acceptable data loss","x":1648,"y":2563,"width":348,"height":50},
		{"id":"e4f6f6f125310613","type":"text","text":"RTO (Recovery Time Objective)","x":1277,"y":2485,"width":316,"height":50},
		{"id":"4e190a427adb3063","type":"text","text":"RPO (Recovery Point Objective)","x":1277,"y":2563,"width":314,"height":50},
		{"id":"e64021e87ecad40b","type":"text","text":"RTO & RPO","x":1033,"y":2538,"width":160,"height":50},
		{"id":"c8650f8f52becd31","type":"text","text":"Business Continuity","x":518,"y":2968,"width":215,"height":50},
		{"id":"392af1a87b626331","type":"text","text":"Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets (VMSS)","x":1031,"y":3514,"width":379,"height":50},
		{"id":"05901174d715bd66","type":"text","text":" is a lightweight software used to back up on-\npremises Windows servers, files, folders, and system state to\nAzure Backup without needing additional infrastructure like\nAzure Backup Server or System Center DPM.","x":1576,"y":3593,"width":531,"height":128},
		{"id":"1f3dc5f217373fc5","type":"text","text":"Key Features of MARS Agent:\n✅ Backs up files, folders, and system state\n✅ Sends encrypted backups to Azure Recovery Services Vault\n✅ Supports long-term retention & incremental backups\n✅ Provides compression for optimized storage usage\n✅ Uses Azure Backup encryption for security","x":1576,"y":3746,"width":544,"height":178},
		{"id":"82d9ad12cd3684e2","type":"text","text":"MARS (Microsoft Azure Recovery Services) Agent","x":1031,"y":3696,"width":443,"height":50},
		{"id":"deefd476e7ade05b","x":2265,"y":-691,"width":157,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Autoscaling"}
	],
